mplement /auth/sms/send, /auth/sms/login, /auth/password/login, /auth/password/change, /auth/password/reset, /auth/token/refresh, /auth/logout, and authenticated phone/WeChat linking in backend/app/api/v1/auth.py, schema/auth.py, service/auth.py, repository/identity.py, provider/sms/__init__.py, provider/factory.py, core/security.py, core/config.py, and core/errors.py. Successful OTP login may create exactly one User only after phone proof and uniqueness locking; password login never creates one. Unknown WeChat openid must return a short-lived bind-required challenge without inserting User/UserWechat; after SMS/password proof it may bind to that same User, while an identity conflict returns merge-required and never auto-merges. JWTs accept auth_method sms|password|wechat plus development only in development/test, include a session identifier, and are rejected when the session is revoked; refresh tokens rotate and replay fails. Password reset/change revokes all old sessions and returns a new session according to policy. Preserve router-level DevAuth non-registration and verification rejection in staging/production. Replace the formal mini-program login flow in miniprogram/pages/login and services/auth.js/api.js with SMS/password tabs, refresh restoration, and optional WeChat linking; keep Seed buttons solely behind explicit LOCAL_PREVIEW in develop and never call /auth/dev/token from a formal action. Schema review must document that 0008 cannot later become a sibling of 0009: if outbox lands first, retarget 0009 to revise 0008; if 0009 lands first, 0008 must revise 0009. Operational rollback is disabling formal features/ai_auto_assign and forward-fixing; downgrade must abort if claimed employees or AUTO assignments make restoration of old NOT NULL constraints unsafe.\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"2. Add identity-neutral house catalog APIs and a formal resident picker\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\backend\\\\\\\\app\\\\\\\\api\\\\\\\\v1\\\\\\\\property_catalog.py\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":\\\"PropertyRepository already has hierarchy list methods, but no HTTP catalog routes exist and the mini-program requires a typed raw house_id.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Add authenticated GET /properties, /properties/{id}/buildings, /buildings/{id}/units, and /units/{id}/houses through new property catalog schemas/service plus api/v1/router.py. Each child query must derive and validate tenant/property ancestry from stored parent records, return only physical catalog fields, exclude resident relations, names, phones, bind requests, and ownership data, and reject cross-hierarchy or inactive-house traversal. Add a minimal authenticated profile update for display_name so the resident sequence is auth -> profile -> catalog. Rework miniprogram/pages/houses into cascading property/building/unit/room selectors; internal IDs may be submitted by selected controls but no formal text field may accept house_id. Continue using the existing POST /resident-bind-requests and manager approve/reject APIs unchanged. Tests must prove catalog responses contain no other resident data, parent-ID splicing fails, an unapproved applicant cannot read house-owned work orders or resident resources, and approval creates the existing ResidentHouseRelation rather than altering House.\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"3. Bind staff identities through controlled invites onto Employee\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\backend\\\\\\\\app\\\\\\\\service\\\\\\\\employee_identity.py\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":\\\"The current admin employee API requires an already-known user_id, and client-supplied identity data can therefore become the binding mechanism.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"In 0009 make employees.user_id nullable while retaining its unique FK for claimed employees; existing non-null rows remain unchanged. Add employee_invites with employee/tenant composite FK, target phone, hashed random token, inviter, expiry, status, claimant, and consumed timestamp. The formal POST /a