 18:     principal: Annotated[Principal, Depends(get_current_principal)],\\n   19: ) -> dict[str, object]:\\n   20:     ordered_grants = sorted(\\n   21:         principal.grants,\\n   22:         key=lambda grant: (\\n   23:             grant.role_code,\\n   24:             grant.scope.scope_type.value,\\n   25:             grant.scope.tenant_id or 0,\\n   26:             grant.scope.property_id or 0,\\n   27:         ),\\n   28:     )\\n   29:     data = MeData(\\n   30:         user_id=principal.user_id,\\n   31:         status=principal.status,\\n   32:         display_name=principal.display_name,\\n   33:         roles=sorted(principal.roles),\\n   34:         permissions=sorted(principal.permissions),\\n   35:         scopes=[\\n   36:             GrantedScopeData(\\n   37:                 role_code=grant.role_code,\\n   38:                 scope_type=grant.scope.scope_type,\\n   39:                 tenant_id=grant.scope.tenant_id,\\n   40:                 property_id=grant.scope.property_id,\\n   41:                 permissions=sorted(grant.permissions),\\n   42:             )\\n   43:             for grant in ordered_grants\\n   44:         ],\\n   45:     )\\n   46:     return success_envelope(request, data.model_dump(mode=\\\"json\\\"))\\n    1: \\\"\\\"\\\"Current Principal response schemas.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    2: \\n    3: from pydantic import BaseModel\\n    4: \\n    5: from app.domain.iam import ScopeType\\n    6: \\n    7: \\n    8: class GrantedScopeData(BaseModel):\\n    9:     role_code: str\\n   10:     scope_type: ScopeType\\n   11:     tenant_id: int | None\\n   12:     property_id: int | None\\n   13:     permissions: list[str]\\n   14: \\n   15: \\n   16: class MeData(BaseModel):\\n   17:     user_id: int\\n   18:     status: str\\n   19:     display_name: str\\n   20:     roles: list[str]\\n   21:     permissions: list[str]\\n   22:     scopes: list[GrantedScopeData]\\n\\nexec\\n\\\"C:\\\\\\\\WINDOWS\\\\\\\\System32\\\\\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\\\\\v1.0\\\\\\\\powershell.exe\\\" -Command \\\"rg -n -S \\\\\\\"mask|redact|password|token|otp|code_hash|authorization\\\\\\\" backend/app/core backend/tests/unit -g '*.py'\\\" in D:\\\\property-ai\\n succeeded in 0ms:\\ncodex\\n{\\\"task_id\\\":\\\"AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"plan\\\",\\\"reviewed_head\\\":\\\"38d3d09bf2e27154c4d106403cbfa9619026755a\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"READY\\\",\\\"actions_or_findings\\\":[{\\\"title\\\":\\\"核验完成，软件切片可立即启动\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":\\\"规格与实际代码均确认四个缺口可在无真实凭证、无持久库迁移的前提下先实现\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"最终计划将把 0009 保持为草案，默认不启用持久环境自动派单，并把真实 Provider 与数据库迁移列为后续人工作业门。\\\"}],\\\"evidence_paths\\\":[\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\reports\\\\\\\\project-handoff.md\\\",\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\docs\\\\\\\\01-PRD.md\\\",\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\docs\\\\\\\\02-ROLES-PERMISSIONS.md\\\",\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\docs\\\\\\\\03-DOMAIN-MODEL.md\\\",\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\docs\\\\\\\\05-AI-DISPATCH-SPEC.md\\\",\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\docs\\\\\\\\06-API-CONTRACT.md\\\"],\\\"unverified\\\":[\\\"本轮未运行任何测试，也未连接或改动 MySQL、Redis、RabbitMQ、MinIO、Milvus。\\\"],\\\"session_note\\\":\\\"正在整理最终 JSON；不会把历史 VIS/Fake 证据升级为正式验收。\\\"}\\ncodex\\n{\\\"task_id\\\":\\\"AUTH-IDENTITY-AI-001\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"plan\\\",\\\"reviewed_head\\\":\\\"38d3d09bf2e27154c4d106403cbfa9619026755a\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"READY\\\",\\\"actions_or_findings\\\":[{\\\"title\\\":\\\"1. Implement official credential authentication and draft migration 0009\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\backend\\\\\\\\alembic\\\\\\\\versions\\\\\\\\20260919_0009_official_auth_identity_dispatch.py\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":\\\"Current authentication supports only Development and WeChat JWTs; SMS/password/session revocation are absent, and unknown WeChat identities silently create Users.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Draft revision 20260919_0009 with down_revision=20260917_0007; do not modify 0001-0007, occupy 0008, or apply it to any persistent database. Add User.profile_completed_at, user_phones with verified history and phone uniqueness, user_passwords with one Argon2id credential per User, sms_challenges with keyed code hash/TTL/attempts/consumed_at, and auth_sessions with hashed rotating refresh tokens, auth_method, expiry, and revocation. Implement atomic Redis send/login throttles through an injectable limiter that fails closed; unit tests must use a fake and must not touch Redis. OTPs must be random per challenge, one-time, retry-limited, never returned by formal APIs, and never logged; the Development SMS provider must be explicitly labeled and test-capturable without becoming real-SMS evidence. Implement /auth/sms/send, /auth/sms/login, /auth/password/login, /auth/password/change, /auth/password/reset, /auth/token/refresh, and /auth/logout across model/identity.py, schema/auth.py, service/auth.py or a focused credential_auth.py, repository/identity.py, provider/sms, provider/factory.py, core/security.py, core/config.py, and core/errors.py. OTP login may create one User only after phone proof and uniqueness locking; password login never creates one. Formal JWTs use auth_method sms|password, a server-checked session identifier, and current database authorization; password reset/change revoke all old sessions and issue a fresh session only after successful verification. Known WeChat bindings may receive session-backed auth_method=wechat tokens; an unknown openid must return bind-required without inserting User/UserWechat, then bind only after an authenticated phone/password session exchanges a fresh WeChat code. Conflicts require later controlled merge, never auto-merge. Update the mini-program login flow to real SMS/password actions, validated /me restoration and refresh rotation; keep Seed login only under explicit LOCAL_PREVIEW and ensure no formal handler calls /auth/dev/token. Router mounting and token verification must independently reject Development Auth outside development/test. If reserved 0008 lands before migration approval, retarget 0009 to revise 0008; otherwise 0008 must later revise 0009—never create sibling heads.\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"2. Add safe house catalog APIs and remove raw house_id from the formal UI\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\backend\\\\\\\\app\\\\\\\\api\\\\\\\\v1\\\\\\\\property_catalog.py\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":\\\"PropertyRepository contains hierarchy queries, but no catalog HTTP routes exist and the current mini-program bind form requires a typed house_id.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Add authenticated GET /properties, /properties/{id}/buildings, /buildings/{id}/units, and /units/{id}/houses using repository/service methods that derive tenant/property ancestry from stored parents rather than trusting client scope. Return only safe physical catalog fields, filter inactive Tenant/House records, and never join or expose resident names, phones, relationships, bind requests, or work orders. Add PATCH /me/profile for display_name and profile completion. Rework pages/houses into cascading property/building/unit/room selectors; the selected internal house ID may be submitted to the unchanged POST /resident-bind-requests API, but no formal text input may accept house_id. Preserve existing manager approve/reject APIs. Tests must prove unauthenticated denial, parent-scope validation, absence of resident data, pending bind state, and that catalog visibility does not authorize work-order creation or resident resources before approval.\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"3. Bind an authenticated User to an existing Employee through a controlled claim\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\backend\\\\\\\\app\\\\\\\\service\\\\\\\\employee_identity.py\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":\\\"POST /admin/employees currently requires client-supplied user_id; no invite or ownership-verification flow exists.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"In 0009 make employees.user_id nullable while retaining the unique FK for claimed employees; existing non-null records remain unchanged. Add employee_invites with BIGINT identity, employee/tenant scope, target phone, hashed random claim token, inviter, expiry, retry/status, claimant, consumed_at, and uniqueness for one active invite per Employee. Permit administrators with current employee:manage scope to create an unbound Employee and separately issue/revoke/resend its invite; keep direct user attachment only in internal Development fixtures. The authenticated claim endpoint must lock invite and Employee, require an active verified UserPhone matching the target, reject expiry/replay/disabled Employee/duplicate binding, and set employee.user_id exactly once. Resolve Role by code STAFF and grant only scopes derived from current EmployeeProperty rows in the same transaction; never accept user_id, role, tenant/property scope, or employee_no as claim authority. Add a mini-program employee-claim page accepting only the opaque invitation. Tests must cover a different authenticated User, employee_no-only input, disabled Employee, expired/replayed invite, duplicate claim, cross-tenant manager, and permission revocation affecting an already-issued session.\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"4. Wire deterministic auto-assignment behind ai_auto_assign\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"D:\\\\\\\\property-ai\\\\\\\\backend\\\\\\\\app\\\\\\\\service\\\\\\\\auto_dispatch.py\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":\\\"AnalysisService writes deterministic recommendations but always stops at PENDING_ASSIGNMENT; WorkOrderAssignment currently requires a human assigned_by_user_id.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Extend 0009 to backfill work_order_assignments.assigned_source=HUMAN, make assigned_by_user_id nullable, add payload_json, and enforce HUMAN requires an actor while AUTO requires assigned_by_user_id NULL. Update response schemas accordingly. Also add ai_call_logs.provider_mode with DEVELOPMENT|PRODUCTION and backfill current rows DEVELOPMENT so Fake and real evidence cannot be mixed. When settin